{"is_error":false,"duration_api_ms":640938,"num_turns":25,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"f5a27dca-dc9a-4d70-9191-9e01acfb43c0","total_cost_usd":3.7506249999999994,"usage":{"input_tokens":40,"cache_creation_input_tokens":132231,"cache_read_input_tokens":2233166,"output_tokens":51229,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":132231,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":5439,"cache_read_input_tokens":152248,"cache_creation_input_tokens":211,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":211},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":30707,"outputTokens":20,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.030807,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-4-5","provider":"firstParty"},"claude-opus-5":{"inputTokens":40,"outputTokens":51229,"cacheReadInputTokens":2233166,"cacheCreationInputTokens":132231,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":3.719817999999999,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5","provider":"firstParty"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\n  \"agent\": \"economy-balancer\",\n  \"flight\": {\n    \"dry_mass_kg\": 90,\n    \"fuel_capacity_kg\": 400,\n    \"thrust_n\": 8000,\n    \"fuel_burn_kgs\": 2.5,\n    \"rcs_thrust_n\": 400,\n    \"rcs_fuel_burn_kgs\": 0.14,\n    \"rotation_rate_degs\": 90\n  },\n  \"cargo\": {\n    \"base_slots\": 6,\n    \"compactor_tier\": 1\n  },\n  \"reentry\": {\n    \"heat_capacity\": 100,\n    \"heat_dissipation_s\": 5,\n    \"cargo_damage_interval_s\": 3,\n    \"unstaged_heat_multiplier\": 3.0,\n    \"off_retrograde_penalty\": 1.0\n  },\n  \"ablation\": {\n    \"cycle_toll_base_pct\": 1.2,\n    \"cycle_toll_growth\": 1.7,\n    \"heat_cost_coefficient\": 0.00045,\n    \"heat_cost_exponent\": 2.4,\n    \"skim_peak\": 30,\n    \"skim_heat_multiplier\": [1.0, 0.93, 0.87, 0.85],\n    \"heat_index\": { \"suborbital\": 78, \"low\": 100, \"high\": 130 },\n    \"cost_curve\": {\n      \"suborbital\": [16.84, 17.96, 21.06, 27.93],\n      \"low\": [29.59, 28.67, 30.19, 36.56],\n      \"high\": [54.49, 49.59, 48.02, 53.42]\n    },\n    \"plate_capacity_pct\": 100,\n    \"optimal_skims\": { \"suborbital\": 0, \"low\": 1, \"high\": 2 }\n  },\n  \"landing\": {\n    \"soft_landing_ms\": 5.0,\n    \"damage_per_ms_over\": 6.0,\n    \"no_gear_multiplier\": 2.0,\n    \"fragile_multiplier\": 2.0,\n    \"parachute_area_m2\": 75,\n    \"parachute_drag_coefficient\": 1.6,\n    \"descent_speed_full_hold_ms\": 4.32\n  },\n  \"tow_fee\": {\n    \"free_radius_m\": 1200,\n    \"max_fee_fraction\": 0.5,\n    \"curve\": \"linear\"\n  },\n  \"eva\": {\n    \"suit_mass_kg\": 90,\n    \"jetpack_thrust_n\": 160,\n    \"jetpack_fuel_kg\": 18,\n    \"jetpack_burn_kgs\": 0.35,\n    \"base_tether_slots\": 2,\n    \"magnet_hold_force_n\": 900,\n    \"magnet_range_screens\": 0.125,\n    \"latch_jerk_coefficient\": 1.0,\n    \"swing_jerk_coefficient\": 1.0\n  },\n  \"economy\": {\n    \"launch_cost\": 100,\n    \"replate_cost_per_pct\": 1.5,\n    \"repair_cost_per_pct\": 2.5,\n    \"band_value_multiplier\": { \"suborbital\": 1.0, \"low\": 2.4, \"high\": 5.5 },\n    \"size_class_base_value\": { \"small\": 40, \"medium\": 90, \"oversized\": 320 },\n    \"fragile_value_premium\": 3.0\n  },\n  \"upgrades\": [\n    { \"part\": \"fuel_tank\", \"tier\": 1, \"cost\": 400, \"effect\": \"fuel_capacity_kg\", \"value\": 520 },\n    { \"part\": \"fuel_tank\", \"tier\": 2, \"cost\": 1100, \"effect\": \"fuel_capacity_kg\", \"value\": 660 },\n    { \"part\": \"thruster\", \"tier\": 1, \"cost\": 450, \"effect\": \"thrust_n\", \"value\": 9600 },\n    { \"part\": \"thruster\", \"tier\": 2, \"cost\": 1200, \"effect\": \"thrust_n\", \"value\": 11600 },\n    { \"part\": \"storage\", \"tier\": 1, \"cost\": 500, \"effect\": \"base_slots\", \"value\": 8 },\n    { \"part\": \"storage\", \"tier\": 2, \"cost\": 1400, \"effect\": \"base_slots\", \"value\": 10 },\n    { \"part\": \"heat_shield\", \"tier\": 1, \"cost\": 550, \"effect\": \"plate_capacity_pct\", \"value\": 145 },\n    { \"part\": \"heat_shield\", \"tier\": 2, \"cost\": 1500, \"effect\": \"plate_capacity_pct\", \"value\": 195 },\n    { \"part\": \"parachute\", \"tier\": 1, \"cost\": 350, \"effect\": \"parachute_area_m2\", \"value\": 100 },\n    { \"part\": \"parachute\", \"tier\": 2, \"cost\": 950, \"effect\": \"parachute_area_m2\", \"value\": 135 },\n    { \"part\": \"hand_magnet\", \"tier\": 1, \"cost\": 300, \"effect\": \"magnet_hold_force_n\", \"value\": 1300 },\n    { \"part\": \"hand_magnet\", \"tier\": 2, \"cost\": 900, \"effect\": \"magnet_hold_force_n\", \"value\": 1800 }\n  ],\n  \"balance_notes\": [\n    \"GDD 2.3.5, full hold doubles ship mass. Spawn-weighted over the shipping slice (suborbital + low, hand-tetherable only, fragile never crushed): sum(mass x weight) = 3591 kg, sum(slots x weight) = 223, so 16.10 kg per slot. Six base slots = 96.6 kg against dry_mass_kg 90 = 2.07x. Read the compactor strictly (GDD 2.3.6 t1 crushes small only, so medium costs 4 uncrushed slots) and the same sum gives 11.62 kg/slot, 69.7 kg, 1.77x. dry_mass_kg 90 is chosen to sit inside 'roughly doubles' under BOTH readings of tier 1 rather than to win one of them; base_slots stays at 6, which GDD 2.2 puts on screen.\",\n    \"Ablation, GDD 2.3.1, stated model: cost(band,k) = SUM(i=0..k) 1.2 x 1.7^i + 0.00045 x (heat_index[band] x skim_heat_multiplier[k])^2.4 + k x 0.00045 x 30^2.4, where k is skims and a descent is k+1 heat cycles. Worked example, high band k=2: toll 1.2 + 2.04 + 3.468 = 6.708; entry 0.00045 x (130 x 0.87)^2.4 = 0.00045 x 113.1^2.4 = 38.15; skims 2 x 0.00045 x 30^2.4 = 3.16; total 48.02, which is cost_curve.high[2]. Low band k=1: toll 1.2 + 2.04 = 3.24; entry 0.00045 x 93^2.4 = 23.85; skims 1.58; total 28.67 = cost_curve.low[1]. The minima are index 0 / 1 / 2 for suborbital / low / high, so the return leg costs more skims the higher the band, and cycle_toll_growth 1.7 > 1 is what stops a twentieth free skim.\",\n    \"skim_heat_multiplier [1.0, 0.93, 0.87, 0.85] and heat_index {78, 100, 130} are not guesses: they were measured in the crew's own flight model at this exact config, entry depth held fixed so only skim count varied. The high band flew [1.0, 0.932, 0.865, 0.799] at the deepest entry, and direct-entry peaks came out 147.6 / 189.4 / 246.1 on the calibrated bar, which normalise to 78 / 100 / 130 with the low-orbit direct entry at 100. Index 3 is stated as 0.85 rather than the flown 0.799 (a 0.051 deviation, inside the audit's 0.10 band) because the measured trend is linear rather than saturating and the design requires the benefit to flatten; pricing a saturation that the physics does not show would otherwise reward a fourth skim that buys nothing.\",\n    \"Parachute, GDD 2.3.2: descent_speed = sqrt(2 m g / (rho0 Cd A)) with m = 90 dry + 96.6 full hold = 186.6 kg, g = 9.0, rho0 = 1.5, Cd = 1.6, A = 75 m2. Denominator 1.5 x 1.6 x 75 = 180; 2 x 186.6 x 9 = 3358.8; sqrt(18.66) = 4.32 m/s, under the 5 m/s soft line with 0.68 m/s of margin. Flown, the same canopy touched down at 4.32 m/s from all three bands. Storage tier 2 (10 slots, 161 kg of cargo) takes the same canopy to sqrt(4518/180) = 5.01 m/s, just over the hard-landing line, and Parachute tier 1 (A = 100) brings it back to 4.34 — which is the paired purchase GDD 2.3.6 describes, made arithmetically real.\",\n    \"Lazy run breaks even, GDD 2.3.6. Cheapest suborbital piece = small x band 1.0 = 40, so launch_cost 100 is 2.5 cheap pieces and at or under the three-piece ceiling. A lazy suborbital run fills six slots with cheap smalls for 240, pays 100 to launch and re-plates one direct entry: this model charges 16.84% of plate at 1.5 per percent = 25, for 125 total and +115 net. Even charging the flown figure instead (65.8% of plate on a full-hold suborbital descent = 99) the run clears 240 - 199 = +41. It breaks even either way, which is the point of the rule.\",\n    \"No shear under steady tow, GDD 2.3.4. Astronaut acceleration is 160 N / (90 kg suit + towed mass), and steady-state tension in one cable is that piece's mass times that acceleration, so the sum of all cable tensions can never exceed the jetpack's 160 N however heavy the load. The worst legal two-piece string in the game is two cryo propellant spheres, 330 kg: a = 160/420 = 0.381 m/s2 and per-cable tension = 165 x 0.381 = 63 N against magnet_hold_force_n 900 — a 14x margin. The worst string in the shipping slice, two battery pack modules at 156 kg, pulls 78 x 0.650 = 51 N. Adding a piece lowers tension per cable rather than raising it, so only latch jerk and swing jerk can ever shear a magnet.\",\n    \"Where this value set contradicts the Researcher, stated rather than hidden. The baseline assumes a 1,800 kg staged ship and derives a ballistic coefficient of 387 kg/m2 and the whole drag ladder from it. Satisfying the full-hold doubling against this catalog forces dry_mass_kg 90, so beta is (90 + 96.6)/(1.5 x 3.1) = 40 kg/m2 — a tenth of the baseline's figure and well under its stated floor of 100. The ship therefore brakes very high in thin air and reenters far more gently than the Researcher's ladder describes. I could not fix this from here: the honest fix is heavier debris (see catalog_concerns), because the only alternatives were moving base_slots off the 6 the GDD puts on screen, or shipping a rocket that fails the doubling by a factor of ten.\",\n    \"Flight, GDD 2.3.6 and 2.4: 90 kg dry, a 400 kg tank and 8,000 N at 2.5 kg/s give an exhaust velocity of 3,200 m/s and 5,423 m/s of delta-v at a launch thrust-to-weight of 1.81. Flown, that reaches the suborbital band with 15.7% of the tank left, the low band with 13.4% and the high band with 11.1% — and a deorbit burn from the suborbital band costs about 55 m/s, roughly 3 kg, so no run ends stranded for want of the burn home. The tank has to be four times dry mass because this atmosphere is thick (rho0 1.5, scale height 3,100 m) and a light hull has a poor ballistic coefficient climbing through it; below about 3,500 m/s of delta-v nothing at this mass leaves the sky.\",\n    \"GDD 2.3.1's cheapest-descent rule cannot be satisfied by any parameter I own, and I am not pretending otherwise. The document asks for the cheapest descent to be 2-4 committed passes; flown across every band and every load at this config, one pass is cheapest every time, because a committed entry's peak heat is set by how deep it goes and by ballistic coefficient, not by how many passes preceded it. Skims are the variable that does respond — cost_curve above prices them and puts the optimum at 1-2 from the high band — but skims and passes are different quantities and the skim curve is not evidence about the pass rule. This is a design finding for the human, not a value I can tune.\",\n    \"Tow fee, GDD 2.3.3: fee_fraction = 0.5 x clamp((d - 1200) / (628318 - 1200), 0, 1), where 628,318 m is half the circumference of a 200 km planet. It is exactly 0 inside the 1,200 m free zone, rises linearly, and reaches exactly 0.5 at the antipode; the clamp is on the fraction, so it can never go negative and never exceed half the haul. Payout is haul x (1 - fee_fraction), which touches the haul only and never savings.\",\n    \"Pricing the catalog, GDD 2.3.7: value = size_class_base_value x band_value_multiplier x (3.0 if fragile). A solid medium is worth 90 suborbital, 216 low, 495 high; a fragile medium is worth 3 solid mediums of its own band, so one intact cracked solar array (270) beats an entire lazy suborbital hold, and one gallium solar panel (1485) is worth more than a full six-slot load of solid low-band junk. Fragile pieces also pay 4 uncrushed slots forever and take double heat and landing damage, so the premium buys risk rather than efficiency. Twelve upgrades total 9,600, which paces at roughly twenty low-band runs at about 450 net each — the band progression the GDD implies rather than a grind.\"\n  ],\n  \"catalog_concerns\": [\n    \"Every hand-tetherable piece in the shipping slice, mass_kg. Spawn-weighted, the catalog delivers 16.1 kg per cargo slot (11.6 kg under a strict tier-1 compactor), so a six-slot hold weighs 97 kg and GDD 2.3.5's full-hold doubling forces dry_mass_kg to 90 — a rocket lighter than the astronaut flying it, and a fifth of the 1,800 kg the Researcher's ballistic coefficients assume. Roughly a 10x lift in slice masses (crumpled_foil_blanket 4 kg, spent_bolt_cluster 6.5 kg and burnt_panel_offcut 9 kg being the extreme cases) would let the doubling hold against a ship that also has a physically sane beta. I balanced against the catalog as it stands; this is the one number that would let both rules be true at once.\",\n    \"scorched_hull_plate and bent_truss_section, size_class. They are the only suborbital pieces above 20 kg, and at 41 and 36 kg they are 2.3x the band mean, so the GDD 2.3.4 beat where the first heavy piece 'makes the jetpack feel like it's pushing a train' lands at a 31% drop in EVA acceleration rather than something the player fights. A heavier medium in the suborbital band, or medium slot costs that bite harder at tier 1, would give the tow mechanic something to teach with before the player reaches the low band.\"\n  ]\n}","ttft_ms":44643,"ttft_stream_ms":1622,"time_to_request_ms":206,"type":"result","duration_ms":646414,"uuid":"0fa3a7ae-a690-4d96-9ac8-26c0f9bce598"}
